{
	"name": "Greater Siren Gull",
	"type": "object",
	"img": "icons/creatures/birds/birds-flock-fly-yellow.webp",
	"system": {
		"description": "<p>Larger than the average seagull, these birds are found around coastal regions and on the open water. As their name suggests their cry is incredibly loud, drawing the attention of both people and other creatures when it sounds the alarm. Adventurers may attempt an Animal Handling check (DC 14) to distract the siren gull or a Stealth check (DC 17) to avoid detection. On a failure, the greater siren gull unleashes a deafening cry that alerts all hostile creatures within 50 feet to the presence of a threat.</p><p>While some who reside in coastal areas can coax greater siren gulls into hanging around warehouses and other establishments to act as natural alarm systems, the birds are often unable to recognize friend from foe. Attempts to cage them and bring them along on the road are often met with burst eardrums and unhappy companions.</p>",
